Let $n={n}$ be a positive even integer. Consider the following system of equations in non-negative real variables $x$ and $y$:
\[
\begin{cases} 
\sqrt[n]{x} + \sqrt[n]{y} = {A} \\
x + y = {B} 
\end{cases}
\]
Let $S$ be the set of all possible values of $x$. Find the sum of the elements in $S$. If $S$ is empty, the sum is 0.
